From 79c11d3b19f63beedd4828c1317b84321c1fe0d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mpv-ht development <mpv-ht@localhost>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:52:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] gpu-next: expose histogram contrast shaping and shadow
 protection

Consolidates the published .76 changes without modifying the final source.
Original: 0053-p-histogram-tone-mapping.patch
Original: 0061-hstm-near-black-protection.patch

diff --git a/DOCS/man/options.rst b/DOCS/man/options.rst
index 33172a9a144573ba4a23d4bac38b8bfd20cf0b0e..cc988a3929319cbe5bc33bb3a8c3491ce5ff3e6e 100644
--- a/DOCS/man/options.rst
+++ b/DOCS/man/options.rst
@@ -7776,6 +7776,30 @@ them.
     Dolby Vision reshape/RPU processing alone does not disable these modes.
     (``--vo=gpu-next`` only)
 
+``--tone-mapping-hstm-strength=<0..100>``
+    Opt-in histogram-shaped tone mapping for the measured ``bt2020-rgb``
+    brightness metric (default: ``0``). Redistributes the existing curve
+    using a smoothed log-P histogram. Strength zero retains normal rendering
+    and does not collect this additional histogram. Requires HDR input and
+    available generic peak measurement. Authored mapping, SDR input and other
+    brightness metrics retain their existing behavior. (``--vo=gpu-next`` only)
+
+``--tone-mapping-hstm-overbrightening=<0..100>``
+    Fraction of HSTM's proposed above-source P increase to retain (default:
+    ``0``). Zero prevents above-source gain in this mapping stage. ``100``
+    retains all proposed lift, bounded to 2x input P and the scalar curve ceiling.
+    ``25`` retains one quarter of the proposed excess, with a maximum gain
+    of 1.25x. It does not add exposure to every pixel. Later ambient or gamut
+    processing can still change brightness. Has no effect at zero HSTM
+    strength. (``--vo=gpu-next`` only)
+
+``--tone-mapping-hstm-near-black-protection=<yes|no>``
+    Preserve the base curve below 0.1 input nits and smoothly introduce
+    histogram slope redistribution through 1 nit (default: ``yes``).
+    ``no`` allows Contrast Shaping down to black. Both choices preserve zero
+    and retain the normal source-gain and peak limits. Has no effect when
+    Contrast Shaping is inactive. (``--vo=gpu-next`` only)
+
 ``--tone-mapping-adaptive-chroma-strength=<0..100>``
     Controls how strongly the ``bt2020-adaptive`` and ``maxrgb-adaptive``
     modes restore chroma removed by libplacebo's normal ITP hull processing.
diff --git a/video/out/gpu/video.c b/video/out/gpu/video.c
